course: dictionary
lesson: 13261
title: Gloom: darkness and sadness
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Gloom means darkness, the dim, shadowy kind you find in a dark room or a dark wood. It can also mean a heavy feeling of sadness, as if all hope has gone. Writers use gloom to set a mood. «The gloom of the attic made the children shiver.» The room is dark, and the children feel uneasy.
explain: Context gives you clues. «Mole lost his way in the gloom of the Wild Wood as the snow fell.» Lost his way and snow tell you it was dark and hard to see, so gloom means darkness here. Ask yourself: what word would fit? Dark? Sad? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Gloom also describes feelings. «After the bad news, a deep gloom settled over the whole family.» Nobody is standing in a dark place. The family feels sad and hopeless. Gloom is a feeling, and that is how you can tell which meaning the writer chose.
fact: Gloom means darkness, or near-darkness, as in a dim room or a dark wood.
fact: Gloom can also mean a feeling of sadness and hopelessness.
fact: «Doom and gloom» means talk that everything will go badly.
fact: Gloom is usually a noun, and you cannot count it: say «some gloom», not «two glooms».
fact: Gloom is a rare verb, but you will meet it as a noun far more often.
exercise: «The gloom of the attic made it hard to read.» What does gloom mean here? | Bright sunshine through a window | A wet, muddy path | *Darkness, where it is hard to see | A loud noise echoing down the stairs
exercise: «After the bad news, the whole family sat in gloom.» What does gloom mean in this sentence? | Loud laughter and games | A fast race round the park | *A feeling of sadness and hopelessness | A dark cupboard full of coats
exercise: Hannah says, «Don't be all doom and gloom, it'll be fine!» What does doom and gloom mean? | A song about the moon | *Talk that everything will go badly | Talk about a sunny holiday | Shouting at the dog
test: «The old church was full of gloom.» Which word is closest in meaning to gloom in this sentence? | Sunshine | Glare | Colour | *Dimness
test: Which sentence uses gloom to mean sadness? | *«A deep gloom fell over the team after they lost.» | «The lamp lit up the gloom of the hall.» | «The team ran fast in the sunshine.»
exam: Which phrase means talk that everything will go badly? | Cold and crisp | Happy and loud | *Doom and gloom | Bright and breezy
